WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:02.933
Last clip Score showed the
reasons for every verdict.

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:05.533
A reason needs data,
and your data has holes.

00:00:05.533 --> 00:00:08.800
Enrichment fills the missing
emails, phones and firmographics,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.700
buys each answer once, and
stops at the cap you set.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:15.967
By the end you'll quote a run, set a
cap, and read coverage for every field.

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:18.600
Enrichment is the engine
that fills empty fields

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.667
on companies and contacts
with provider verified values,

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:22.700
and keeps them fresh.

00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:26.133
Leo pulls the hot accounts and
finds half the phone numbers blank.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:29.067
Buying them by hand means paying
twice for the same answer,

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.567
and no value carries a date.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:33.933
Enrichment prices the job
first, and dates every answer.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.267
First, the waterfall.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.900
For each empty field, Enrichment asks
the first provider in your binding.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.267
If that one has nothing, it asks the
next, and it stops at the first answer.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:45.300
Providers are reached through
looot with your organization's key,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.900
so connecting looot once is enough.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.800
An answer is bought once and cached,
so the same question never costs twice.

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:52.667
Second, it fills empty fields only.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.667
A lookup never overwrites a
value already on the record.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.533
When a newer enriched value differs,

00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:00.467
the company or contact page
shows Newer enriched values,

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.567
with Propose update.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:04.800
The approval shows the old and
new value, provenance, confidence,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.467
the reason, and an undo. A value a
person typed needs an explicit confirm,

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.533
and only a person can approve it.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.700
Third, freshness.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.500
Every value is stamped with when it
was verified, how long it stays fresh,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.667
its confidence and its provider.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.267
By default an email stays
fresh about three months,

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.233
and a phone and firmographics about six.

00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:24.533
Override any window in the
enrichment policy definition.

00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:26.267
A refresh re-checks only stale values

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.100
that Enrichment wrote and nobody edited.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.600
If a provider has nothing,
the old value stays,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.033
and it tries again a week later.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.367
Providers fail. On an outage,
a timeout or a server error,

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.900
the lookup falls through to the
next provider in the binding.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.167
Every attempt is recorded.
Here's the honest part.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:44.000
A fallback after a timeout can mean two
providers were asked for one lookup.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.833
The attempt log shows it,
so a fallback is never free.

00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:48.100
Money has three guards.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.333
Every run is quoted first,
an estimate with no spend.

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:52.833
Each binding carries a
price ceiling per lookup.

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:54.867
And the owner or an
admin sets a monthly cap.

00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:57.467
When money is limited, the best
accounts are enriched first,

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.133
and cached answers still run free.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:02.333
In the console: Engines, Enrichment,
where you change the cap.

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:05.533
Or ask your agent: "How much of the
monthly enrichment cap is left? "

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.167
Now run it.

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.900
In the console: Engines, Enrichment
shows the mode, the fill rate,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.733
spend this month, your bindings, the
freshness windows and the run history.

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:15.800
Or ask your agent: "Quote filling
missing emails for the hot list".

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.467
You'll see an estimate and no spend.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.633
Pro move: quote first, then run
with the quote as your ceiling.

00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:22.967
Ask your agent: "Run
enrichment for the hot list,

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:25.367
but stay under the estimate".
Or let a play do it.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.367
The weekly account
enrichment play is capped,

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:30.667
and the enrich on create play
refuses to run without a monthly cap.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:33.967
In Dry Mode, a run returns the
estimate and attempts no lookup.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.333
The dashboard answers one
question: how complete are we?

00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:39.367
You see the fill rate, the spend,
and coverage for each field,

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.433
with how many values are fresh
and how many have gone stale.

00:02:42.433 --> 00:02:44.600
Or ask your agent: "What
is our enrichment coverage,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.033
and which values are stale? "

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.500
It improves without guessing.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.467
Freshness windows and confidence
decide what gets bought again,

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.267
so spend goes to values going
stale and fields still empty.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.733
You set the provider order in the binding,

00:02:55.733 --> 00:02:57.233
and the attempt log shows who answered.

00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:59.433
Change either in the
console, or ask your agent,

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:00.900
and a different person signs.

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:03.533
Enrichment feeds the rest.
Fit fields sharpen Score.

00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:06.433
Backfilled domains help
Merges spot duplicates.

00:03:06.433 --> 00:03:08.400
Routing reads country and size,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.900
and Outreach personalizes
with what's now known.

00:03:10.967 --> 00:03:13.967
Not built yet: the title,
seniority and job change steps.

00:03:13.967 --> 00:03:16.667
They're planned, and nothing
you've seen here depends on them.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.933
You may be thinking: an engine with
a budget will quietly spend it.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:23.467
It can't. Every run is quoted first,
each lookup has a price ceiling,

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.100
and the monthly cap stops the rest.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.167
In Dry Mode, nothing is looked up at all.

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:30.367
To recap: The waterfall
stops at the first answer,

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.767
and a person approves
every change to a value.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.433
Quote first, buy once, date every value.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.867
Every gap is now filled at a price
you set, with a date on every value.

00:03:38.867 --> 00:03:42.933
Quote one run from Engines, Enrichment.
Up next, Signals and intent,

00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:45.567
where the market starts
talking about your accounts.
